# Template. On first run this is copied to ~/.ssh/config.local, which git does
# not track. Put real work hostnames in that copy. This file itself is
# committed to a public repo, so anything written here is published.
#
# Hostnames and IdentityFile paths only. Never key material.
#
# The tracked ~/.ssh/config Includes this at its top, because ssh is
# first-match-wins and a block placed lower could never override an earlier one.

# Host your-work-alias
#   HostName git.internal.example.com
#   AddKeysToAgent yes
#   IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519_work
